<h1>Using the wastebasket class</h1>

<p>The <a href="../classes/html/classwastebasket.html">wastebasket class</a> provides a garbage collection object.  Arbitrary arrays of primitives, objects, and arrays of objects can be attached to it and deleted at a later date.</p>

<p>This is useful for holding on to dependencies of an object until the object no longer needs them.  For example, a function might create several related objects, return one of them, and attach the others to a wastebasket.  The caller can use the returned object and then empty the wastebasket to clean everything up at once.</p>

<p>The wastebasket class is targeted for use with the MVC classes, but it can be used in non-MVC projects as well.</p>

